title: Separated unto God – Liberty and the Weaker Brother
description: The Christian walk, part two: God is a God of separation, come out from among them, righteous Lot, keeping the spirit of the command, in the world but not of it, and the liberty we have in Christ with care for the weaker brother, from the teachings on the walk.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-walk-separation.html

# The second of five decks on studies/data/topics/walk.json: "Separation from the world" and its balance,
# "Liberty and the weaker brother". The teachings on wine and strong drink are kept for their own deck.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "his does" -> "his foes" (6815), "out ability" -> "our ability" (13462), "Aestheticism" -> "Asceticism" (11449).

=== Introduction
--- Separated unto God [title]
overline: Doctrine · The walk
heading: Separated unto God
sub: The walk, part two: separation from the world, and the liberty we have in Christ.
refs: 2 Corinthians 6:17; 1 Peter 2:9; Romans 14:13; Galatians 5:13
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 12390
--- God is a God of separation
lead: God is a God of separation. The Bible has example after example of division, separating one thing from another.
p: Day from night. The creatures after their own kind. The descendants of Seth, the sons of God that called upon the name of the Lord, and the children of men who did not. Noah and his perfect generations from fallen man. Abraham out of Ur. Jacob and Esau. Out of Egypt and back in the land. The tares from the wheat. Sheep from goats.
big: 1 Peter 2:9 | mark: a peculiar people

# from 17717, 16425
--- Separated unto His gospel
lead: The Christian life is one of separation. Of leaving behind the things of this world, and the wickedness men do, separated unto His gospel, and proclaiming His truth.
big: 2 Corinthians 6:17 | mark: come out from among them, and be ye separate
p: This doesn't mean that if you had or have struggles with sin that you're done, defiled and unusable. It means the more we purify ourselves, the more we walk in the Spirit, the more useful we are as a vessel in His holy service.

=== Come out from among them
# from 4147
--- Be ye not unequally yoked
kicker: Come out from among them
scripture: 2 Corinthians 6:14-16 | mark: Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers
p: Many apply this to marriage and being with an unbelieving spouse, but it's far more broad than that. So many Christians, in desperation and fear, join forces and ally themselves with unbelievers.
p: How can one set of unbelieving, Christ-hating, worldly materialists help save us from another? They can't. All they can do is lead us to a place that brings offense and blame to our ministry.

# from 15158
--- Jehoshaphat yoked with Ahab
kicker: Come out from among them
lead: How often in our Christian life do we find ourselves in a similar situation? Where maybe we seek peace, or not to offend, or a fruitful partnership with someone who is unsaved, and wicked.
p: Jehoshaphat, wearing his kingly robes at Ahab's suggestion, becomes the target of the Syrians. If not for calling out to the Lord, he would have been slain then and there. The wicked taking advantage of mistaken loyalty to save their own skin is one of the biggest risks of being allied with them.
big: 2 Chronicles 19:2 | mark: Shouldest thou help the ungodly, and love them that hate the LORD

# from 6815, 2666
--- Not partakers of other men's sins
kicker: Come out from among them
p: Abram refuses spoils from the King of Sodom, not wanting anything from that wicked man. He did what he did because it was right. Staying out of the war, not getting entangled in commitments with the wicked, but defending brethren and having faith in God to destroy our enemies ([[Genesis 14:22-23]]).
p: The Bible says that even by his presence and holding the coats of those stoning Stephen to death, Saul was “consenting unto his death” ([[Acts 8:1]]). Giving even passive consent to sin is a sin.
big: 1 Timothy 5:22 | mark: neither be partaker of other men’s sins: keep thyself pure
read: app:doctrine-walk~4147 | Be ye not unequally yoked
read: app:doctrine-walk~15158 | Jehoshaphat yoked with wicked Ahab
