read: app:doctrine-walk~13349 | All things are not expedient
read: app:doctrine-walk~16425 | Separated chambers
read: app:doctrine-walk~16786 | Constant vigilance to keep the people separate

=== In the world, not of it
# from 11667
--- Bloom where the Lord has planted you
kicker: In the world, not of it
scripture: Jeremiah 9:2 | mark: Oh that I had in the wilderness a lodging place of wayfaring men
p: This same impulse is given to Christians today. To flee the world, to get to a redoubt in the wilderness. But, like the prophets, and like Christ Himself, we go to Jerusalem. We can't be a light to others if we are hidden in the woods.
take: And so we are in the world, not of it. We are supposed to bloom where the good Lord has planted us.

# from 7461, 16745
--- The world hates an evil report
kicker: In the world, not of it
p: Joseph brings his father an evil report of his brothers, and they hate him for it ([[Genesis 37:2]] · [[Genesis 37:4]]). Much the same way today the world hates a faithful Christian for the reminder of their sin we bring.
big: John 3:20 | mark: every one that doeth evil hateth the light
p: In our Christian life, we may experience initial scoffing by our friends, family and neighbors. People who doubt our conversion because they know us. The old man. As Nehemiah did, keep building the wall while the mockers scoff ([[Nehemiah 4:3]]).

# from 9713
--- Blessed with separation
kicker: In the world, not of it
lead: Almost all of the provocations meant to anger us happen in the realms they control, which are wicked and worldly.
p: Most of what they “ruin” isn't something we should be consuming or engaged in to begin with. By turning you off or excluding you from the things they control, they are essentially blessing you with separation. God is using these things to bring you out of Sodom.
p: By subjecting you to their provocations, rather than anger, be glad that you now have reason to leave behind their sin, and better serve God, as a separate people, a holy nation.

# from 14937, 4690
--- When family despises your walk
kicker: In the world, not of it
p: Michal looks upon David, gladly worshipping the Lord, and despises him in her heart ([[1 Chronicles 15:29]]). In a like manner, we may experience this as saved believers, where a family member resents our going to church, reading the Bible, cleaning up our life.
big: Ephesians 5:8 | mark: walk as children of light
p: Walking in the light, where the sins of the dark are made manifest. Making the most of our short time here, in these evil days.
