=== Liberty and the weaker brother
# from 1151, 10990
--- Receive the weak in faith
kicker: Liberty and the weaker brother
scripture: Romans 14:1-3 | mark: Him that is weak in the faith receive ye, but not to doubtful disputations
p: Romans 14 is addressing brothers in Christ, weak in the faith they may be, who add as sin things not inherently sinful, to their own judgement in service to God. And it's twisted by some who take the liberty found in Christ as a license to sin.
p: A person weak in the faith may hold themselves to a higher standard than the Bible calls for, that we being more stable in the faith may see as silly. Paul is warning not to use the occasion to argue with them.

# from 3771, 3826
--- Not at the expense of others
kicker: Liberty and the weaker brother
big: 1 Corinthians 8:9 | mark: lest by any means this liberty of yours become a stumblingblock to them that are weak
p: Knowing it's nothing but meat, and the pagan practice silly, we could in good conscience eat the sacrifice and give all blessing and honor to God. But if that thing done in our knowledge were to cause the weaker man to sin or not come to the faith of the one true God, we shouldn't do it.
p: When we act agreeable to others to win them to the gospel, that is not the same as accepting wickedness in our presence. Being mature enough in the word to understand the distinction is one of the goals of consuming the word daily.

# from 10991, 10992
--- Who art thou that judgest?
kicker: Liberty and the weaker brother
big: Romans 14:4-5 | mark: Who art thou that judgest another man’s servant; Let every man be fully persuaded in his own mind
p: And by the same token, those weaker in the faith should learn not to judge another's walk, if it is keeping with the spirit of the law, but maybe not to your liking.
p: Those who don't strive as you strive need your encouragement. Not your scorn, lest we think better of ourselves than we ought. Save admonishment for actual clear doctrines, not your opinions.

# from 11449, 11681, 11683
--- Meat, drink and holy days
kicker: Liberty and the weaker brother
big: Colossians 2:16 | mark: Let no man therefore judge you in meat, or in drink, or in respect of an holyday
p: The vain philosophy of men, as well as the old testament strictures, have no power over we who are saved by faith in Christ. Voluntary humility, asceticism, the denial of self for the purpose of self-righteousness: *Touch not; taste not; handle not*.
p: Jeremiah 10 is about graven images decked with silver and gold, not decorating your house at Christmas. No one can be tricked into sin. If the heart is blessing the day in Christ, then it is of Christ.
refs: Jeremiah 10:3-5; Isaiah 60:13; Romans 14:6

# from 13245
--- From glory to glory
kicker: Liberty and the weaker brother
big: 2 Corinthians 3:17-18 | mark: where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty; changed into the same image from glory to glory
p: We have the Spirit of the Lord so we are at liberty. We aren't judged by the law. But even so, in liberty, and beholding the glory of God towards us, by walking in that Spirit, we see our own selves transformed by His glory. We are changed by it if we choose to be.
